      "abstract": "Kant\u2019s moral theology was a subject of intense debate in the early reception of Kant\u2019s philosophy. At the same time, Kant\u2019s notion of practical postulation held considerable interest for Fichte, Schelling, and Hegel. What I seek to show is the systematic connection of these two facts: examination of the ways in which Kant\u2019s postulates of pure practical reason exposed the Kantian system to criticism sheds light, I argue, on some of the fundamental moves made by the German Idealists in their transformation of Kant\u2019s philosophy.",
